<title>USA: Jones Medical sees Q2 eps of $0.20/shr.</title>
<headline>Jones Medical sees Q2 eps of $0.20/shr.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jones Medical Industries Inc said it expects to earn about $0.20 per share for the second quarter on sales that are below analysts' expectations.</p>
<p>The lower sales stem from aggressive wholesale buying of Tapazole and Levoxyl during March, in anticipation of an April 1 price hike, the company said.</p>
<p>The lower sales will result in lower gross margins for the quarter, the company added.</p>
</text>
